This directory is published as the site root, and is empty on purpose.

Nothing should be served statically: every request has to reach the api
function so that authentication covers the page as well as the API. With an
empty publish directory that happens naturally - no static file matches, so
the catch-all redirect takes over.

The alternative, force = true on /*, also captures /.netlify/functions/*,
which makes the background and scheduled functions unreachable.
